I found these by searching the docs folder for route model binding terms. I didn't open the files to check their contents.

The likely cause is in your route. With `Route::get('locationtypes/{id}', ...)`, the `{id}` parameter doesn't match the `$locationType` argument in `show()`. Laravel's implicit binding matches the route parameter name to the variable name, so it never loads the model. When you changed the route to `{locationType}`, it started working. These documents cover implicit binding, `resolveRouteBinding`, and how resources serialize a model.

